WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everyone.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.501
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.734
You're here. "The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:10.701
♪♪

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.934
Happy Halloween, everybody!

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:15.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:17.200
You can tell I'm in
the Halloween spirit.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.934
I've been wearing my
Jimmy Kimmel costume

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.601
for almost two months now.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:22.834
Well, this is fun.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.033
Earlier tonight, President Biden
and the First Lady

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.000
welcomed trick-or-treaters
to The White House

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.934
for the first fully in-person
Halloween celebration

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.434
since the pandemic.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.067
Yep, Halloween was back at
The White House,

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.934
and it was
a nice chance to reuse

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.000
Melania's Christmas decorations.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.767
Trick-or-treaters were psyched.

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.701
Every kid went home with
a bag of candy.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.501
It was different than
the last administration,

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.634
when every kid went home with a
bag of classified documents.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.167
[ As Trump ] Only take one.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.801
Only take one
classified document.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.667
Meet you at Mar-a-Lago."

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:03.934
[ Normal voice ]
I read that some of the

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.501
most popular Halloween candies
this year are

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:09.200
Reese's Peanut Butter Cups,
KitKats, and Snickers.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.067
But there are
some candies out there

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.834
that people don't like as much.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.167
Tariq, do you think
you can give us

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.234
some tips on
which candies to avoid?

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:19.267
-Do I? Hit it.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:22.200
♪♪

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.501
♪ Candy corn,
you can take a back seat ♪

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.167
♪ You're tacky, waxy,
bad as rancid crab meat ♪

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.133
♪ Necco Wafer,
you're inedible rock ♪

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.767
♪ Just a swole-ass Smartie
that takes like chalk ♪

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.300
♪ Don't even get me started on
Good &amp; Plentys ♪

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.934
♪ You taste like pennies,
more like Bad &amp; Too Manys ♪

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.067
♪ And Milk Duds? ♪

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.501
♪ Get away from me ♪

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.834
♪ Won't get you out of my teeth
until Christmas Eve ♪

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.167
♪ And Jujubes,
you get an ew from me ♪

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.033
♪ I'd rather chew blue cheese
mixed with prune juice, please ♪

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.067
♪ And, Dots, how 'bout not? ♪

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.434
♪ You can rot in the box ♪

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.834
♪ Gimme Twix, Junior Mints,
anything but a dot ♪

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.501
♪ Gimme Reese's, Snickers,
Crunch, or Runts ♪

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.701
♪ But gimme Laffy Taffy,
and I'll punch your guts ♪

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:59.300
♪ I'll take anything
out of desperation ♪

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.200
♪ If the only other option
is a box of raisins ♪

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.567
-Oh, come on, now!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:08.634
Come on. Come on, now.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.834
-Oh, my!
-That's amazing.

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.801
The greatest!
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:16.000
-Tariq Trotter! Come on.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:22.300
Hey, guys, I saw that,
this weekend,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.868
former president Obama
was campaigning in Michigan.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.767
And when he started talking
about getting older,

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.200
some women in the crowd
chimed in.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.734
Take a look at this.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:32.968
-I have to admit that sometimes
going out on the campaign trail

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.934
feels a little harder
than it used to.

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:39.434
Not just because
I'm older and grayer.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:45.067
-Fine little...
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.467
-I don't know
if y'all heard that.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:47.934
Said I was still fine.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.968
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:53.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.334
Fine?

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:58.067
Then Michelle was like,
"Yeah, I think we're done with

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.167
the campaign speeches, alright?"

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:03.367
He's like, "I'm Barack Obama.
I approved this message."

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.367
That's the one difference
between Obama and Biden.

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:07.934
When Obama is onstage,
people are like, "He is fine."

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.968
And when Biden is onstage,
people are like, "He's fine."

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.434
"He's fine."

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.434
That's right -- the Democrats
have deployed Obama

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:19.334
on the campaign trail.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:20.801
Tell me you're nervous
about the midterms

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.667
without telling me you're
nervous about the midterms.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:24.968
Some business news.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.701
In Elon Musk's first round of
layoffs at Twitter,

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:31.834
he reportedly plans to fire
25% of the company's workforce.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:34.100
Meanwhile, Facebook said,
"We're hiring."

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.934
Everyone was like, "No, thanks."

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:39.868
But Twitter is actually
trying to hire replacements,

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.601
and we found some questions
on the application

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:42.968
that Elon Musk is sending out.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.434
And here are
some of the questions.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.901
They're very interesting here.
Let's check some of these out.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.100
First one says...

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.567
-Wow!
-Next up, there's...

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.267
After that, it asked...

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.868
"V-Bucks, please." Yep.
Then it says...

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.868
These are odd questions.

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:23.033
-Yeah.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.367
-And, finally, it asks...

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.133
-Wow!

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.601
-I don't know.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.000
Good luck.

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.334
But did you see this, though?

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:36.167
Elon Musk tweeted something that
was considered misinformation

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.334
and then deleted it later

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.167
because it was
a false conspiracy theory.

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:42.400
Which is awkward when
you're the owner of Twitter.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.834
Here was the e-mail
that Musk received. It said...

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's a lot to figure...

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:12.234
Meanwhile, I saw that to reduce
the amount of misinformation

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.200
on their platform,
YouTube will now let

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.501
doctors and nurses
apply for their videos

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:17.868
to be marked as reliable.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.033
-Ooh!
-Yeah.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.267
YouTube finally looked at
all their misinformation

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:22.400
on their site and said...

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.934
-Ain't nobody got time for that.

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.934
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:33.167
So now people who
post fake information online

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.601
are freaking out, like...

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:36.334
-[ Bleating loudly ]

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:38.334
-Because if they keep
spreading lies,

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.667
YouTube might step in
and stop them, kind of like...

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:43.334
-The question is, how do
democracies respond to...

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:45.067
-And what will it mean for...

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:48.100
-But people need to know which
sources to trust

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.901
or they could fall
for anything, like...

00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:55.801
-Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:59.367
-Or they might jump to wrong
conclusions, kind of like...

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:02.167
♪♪

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.300
-♪ Sail ♪

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:08.000
-So if you're spreading
misinformation,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.968
it's got to come down,
kind of like...

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.400
And, please, always make sure
your sources are reliable

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.734
or nothing you say
will make sense, kind of like...

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:25.567
-What do you think?
-I like turtles.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:26.968
-Yeah, there you go.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:30.000
I hope that helped.
I hope that helped everybody.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.767
"Hi, Billy."
-"Hey, Ron."

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.767
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:38.801
[ Imitates crashing ]

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:41.868
"Hey, Ron."
-"Hey, Billy."

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.467
Some more business news.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:46.434
Spirit Airlines just revealed
upgraded, larger seats

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:48.067
that they're adding to
their new planes.

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:49.367
-Ooh!

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:53.367
-They're all on the wing,
but, still, it's something.

00:06:53.367 --> 00:06:54.667
That's right -- larger seats.

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:56.667
But to maximize profits,
they'll make you

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:59.067
spoon with another passenger.

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:00.434
Well, get this.

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:03.567
I heard that nearly 150,000
pounds of chicken patties

00:07:03.567 --> 00:07:05.701
sold at Costco
have been recalled

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.801
'cause there might be
plastic in it.

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:10.200
150,000 pounds of chicken.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.200
Thankfully, at Costco,
that's just one package.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:19.968
Finally, some thieves
in Georgia were arrested

00:07:19.968 --> 00:07:21.601
after police found them
by following

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:24.033
a trail of candy wrappers
in the woods.

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:25.901
The judge must have had fun
with the story

00:07:25.901 --> 00:07:28.100
because their bail was
100 grand.

00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:31.634
I just want to say
to all the parents at home

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.400
eating your children's
Halloween candy,

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:34.968
you know what
you're doing is wrong.

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:36.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.567
Yeah, you can tell
today is November 1st

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:40.367
'cause all the Spirit Halloweens
have gone back

00:07:40.367 --> 00:07:43.501
to being abandoned
Sears Outlets.

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.033
Let's get to some news.

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:48.634
Guys, the midterm elections
are just one week away.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.968
That's right. In one week,
we'll know who gets the House,

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.400
the Senate, and the upper hand
at Thanksgiving.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:07:54.968 --> 00:07:56.501
You can tell
the midterms are close

00:07:56.501 --> 00:07:58.767
when the fundraising e-mails
are in all caps.

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:00.934
"JIMMY, I NEED 10 DOLLARS NOW!"

00:08:00.934 --> 00:08:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:04.367
And get this --
as if the midterms

00:08:04.367 --> 00:08:06.567
weren't already crazy enough,
apparently the country

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:10.033
is facing
a paper-ballot shortage.

00:08:10.033 --> 00:08:11.901
Right now the MyPillow guy
is yelling at a tree

00:08:11.901 --> 00:08:14.834
for rigging the election.

00:08:14.834 --> 00:08:16.501
A paper-ballot shortage.

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:18.701
Now on Election Day,
you have to close the curtain

00:08:18.701 --> 00:08:20.133
and just yell for
who you're voting for.

00:08:20.133 --> 00:08:23.334
Like, "Republican, Republican,
Democrat, Republican!"

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:25.200
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.868
Well, President Biden
is working hard

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:29.567
to give Democrats a final
push before the election.

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:32.601
Starting today, he's appearing
at campaign rallies in Florida,

00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:36.734
New Mexico, California,
Pennsylvania, and Maryland.

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:39.200
Yeah, if a jet-lagged
79-year-old

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.634
can't rally the Democrats,
nothing can.

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:44.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:46.400
[ Applause ]

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.501
Yeah, today,
Biden was in Florida,

00:08:48.501 --> 00:08:50.767
which is a tough place
for Democrats.

00:08:50.767 --> 00:08:52.701
I mean, right now
one Democrat in Florida

00:08:52.701 --> 00:08:54.834
is losing to an alligator
with a mullet.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:57.200
It's interesting.
Well, this is wild --

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.868
I read that Republicans
are expecting

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:00.901
former President Trump
to be indicted

00:09:00.901 --> 00:09:03.367
soon after Election Day.

00:09:03.367 --> 00:09:04.868
Yeah, it feels like
the political version

00:09:04.868 --> 00:09:06.133
of waiting to break up
with someone

00:09:06.133 --> 00:09:07.734
until after the holidays.

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:09.734
It's like, "Ah, just..."

00:09:09.734 --> 00:09:12.167
Yeah, Trump could be indicted
for the holidays,

00:09:12.167 --> 00:09:15.968
which sounds kind of like
a Christmas movie on MSNBC.

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:18.167
Speaking of
the former president,

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:20.000
Supreme Court Chief Justice
John Roberts

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.167
just temporarily blocked
Congress

00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:26.033
from obtaining years of Trump's
federal income tax returns.

00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:28.033
Yep, Trump was so excited,
he started chugging ketchup

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:31.901
like he'd won the Indy 500.
He's like...

00:09:31.901 --> 00:09:34.968
Switching gears, now that Elon
Musk has taken over Twitter,

00:09:34.968 --> 00:09:37.634
he apparently also wants
to bring back Vine

00:09:37.634 --> 00:09:39.234
to compete with TikTok.

00:09:39.234 --> 00:09:42.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:42.534 --> 00:09:43.868
I like it.
I think it'd be a great idea.

00:09:43.868 --> 00:09:45.334
I also think it would be great
if they had a feature

00:09:45.334 --> 00:09:47.734
where you could fast-forward
videos to get to the best part.

00:09:47.734 --> 00:09:49.133
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:49.133 --> 00:09:51.868
For example,
you could skip this part...

00:09:51.868 --> 00:09:53.267
Yeah.

00:09:53.267 --> 00:09:55.968
And go --
go right to this part.

00:09:55.968 --> 00:09:57.200
-Ow!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.033
-Yeah.

00:09:59.033 --> 00:10:01.033
[ Applause ]

00:10:03.601 --> 00:10:05.334
I didn't know the first part
was that fast.

00:10:05.334 --> 00:10:07.033
[ Laughter ]
-It snuck up on you.

00:10:07.033 --> 00:10:09.467
- Yeah, yeah, yeah,
it was actually -- you could --

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:11.167
you could actually
watch the whole video.

00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.901 --> 00:10:15.033
That makes no sense.

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:17.767
Let me give you an example here.
You skip this part...

00:10:20.033 --> 00:10:21.968
Yeah.
And go right to this part.

00:10:24.501 --> 00:10:26.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.534
That's what I want to see. I --

00:10:29.534 --> 00:10:31.701
Let's give one more example.
You can skip this part...

00:10:33.133 --> 00:10:34.901
Yeah, and go right to this part.

00:10:34.901 --> 00:10:37.133
-[ Screaming ]

00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:40.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:40.968 --> 00:10:43.667
♪♪

00:10:43.667 --> 00:10:46.868
-Flipper!
-Wow.

00:10:46.868 --> 00:10:49.434
Guys, get this.
The makers of Ring doorbell

00:10:49.434 --> 00:10:52.834
are about to release
their first car alarm.

00:10:52.834 --> 00:10:54.267
I'm not sure how helpful it is.

00:10:54.267 --> 00:10:56.100
All it does is let you watch
someone steal your car.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.801
You go, "Oh..."

00:10:57.801 --> 00:11:01.667
[ Laughter ]

00:11:01.667 --> 00:11:03.934
Hey, I saw that TV ratings
for this year's World Series

00:11:03.934 --> 00:11:07.167
between the Astros and the
Phillies are the best in years.

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:09.100
So, naturally,
a lot of the brands

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.868
want to get their message out
to such a big audience.

00:11:10.868 --> 00:11:12.367
But I was surprised
at some of this year's

00:11:12.367 --> 00:11:14.901
World Series sponsors.
Watch this I saw.

00:11:14.901 --> 00:11:18.200
-The MLB World Series
is brought to you by Twitter...

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:33.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:37.167 --> 00:11:39.067
-And finally, in China,

00:11:39.067 --> 00:11:41.400
the winner
of a $30-million lottery jackpot

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.601
is not telling his family
about it

00:11:43.601 --> 00:11:45.868
'cause he doesn't want them
to get lazy.

00:11:45.868 --> 00:11:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:48.834 --> 00:11:50.934
It's just gonna be weird
on family vacations

00:11:50.934 --> 00:11:53.501
when the kids are like, "Why is
dad in first class without us?"

00:11:54.834 --> 00:11:56.634
It seems like there's so much
going on right now.

00:11:56.634 --> 00:11:58.767
Everyone's gearing up for
the midterms.

00:11:58.767 --> 00:12:01.367
The World Series is heating up.

00:12:01.367 --> 00:12:05.000
The top-10 songs in the country
are all by Taylor Swift.

